<title>USA: Providence and Worcester buys hauling right.</title>
<headline>Providence and Worcester buys hauling right.</headline>
<dateline>WORCESTER, Mass. 1996-10-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Providence and Worcester Railroad Co said Monday it has acquired from Conrail Inc exclusive rights to haul sand and stone between New Haven, Conn., and Fresh Pond Junction in Freemont, N.Y.</p>
<p>The company estimates the acquisition will result in about 2,000 additional carloads. The company said it currently handles about 29,000 conventional carloads and 40,000 Intermodal containers a year.</p>
